  "id": "levomepromazine",
  "term": "levomepromazine",
  "definition": "Levomepromazine is a phenothiazine, typical antipsychotic drug with sedating, anxiety-reducing, anti-nausea, pain-relieving, and antipsychotic effects. Its exact action is not fully known, but it appears to work by blocking several types of receptors in the central nervous system, including dopamine, serotonin, histamine, cholinergic, and adrenergic receptors.",
